## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Google AI developer docs describe Gemini 2.5 Flash (`gemini-2.5-flash`) as a deprecated price-performance model with 1,048,576-token input limit, 65,536-token output limit, multimodal inputs (text/image/video/audio), text output, thinking/tool-use capabilities, and knowledge cutoff January 2025. Artificial Analysis lists Gemini 2.5 Flash (Non-reasoning) with Intelligence Index and task-level aggregates unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot.
- Searched accessible sources (Google AI docs, Artificial Analysis, OpenRouter) but did not find extractable, verifiable numeric benchmark scores (e.g. GPQA, SWE-bench, HLE, MMMU, Terminal-Bench, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.) clearly attributable to the exact `gemini-2.5-flash` model/ID in the fetched content.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

